That means it needs its proper allocation.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:40.440
In today's world, if you
are a massive company

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:43.740
in the UK market, between
Instagram and Facebook,

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.840
you are getting to a
shocking amount of people

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.490
at a very low cost.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.820
But meanwhile, they wanna deck out

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.970
a double-decker bus for
awareness, you know?

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:56.980
So, I would say this.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.570
Nobody is allocating the
appropriate amount of money

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.790
to Facebook and Instagram,
given how underpriced it is.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:07.790
Do I believe that Pepsi and
Puma, in the UK or in Europe

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.210
should spend 50, 60% of their money

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.240
just on Facebook and Instagram?

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.233
The answer is yes.

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:15.710
Should they do a lot of
the other things they do?

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.320
Yup, but they should cut the
budgets on all those things,

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:20.270
so that they can afford the 50 to 60%

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.010
on Facebook and Instagram.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:22.960
I believe that.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.377
(bass music)

